From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: forget the tx descriptor pages once they are freed

ath11k_nss_tx_desc_mem_free() tests tx_desc_paddr[] to see whether a
page is allocated but only clears tx_desc_vaddr[] after freeing it, so a
second call - a failed bring-up followed by the regular teardown, or a
firmware recovery - frees the same DMA memory again.

Clear the address too.

Taken from Julius Bairaktaris' openwrt-nss-edma (nss-edma-rework), where
it is part of 199-002.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4224,6 +4224,7 @@
 				  ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i],
 				  ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i]);
 		ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i] = NULL;
+		ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i] = 0;
 	}
 
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_NSS, "allocated tx desc mem freed\n");
